Conventions: Standards

Purpose:
  Defines conventions for .sdd file structure, content, and
  maintenance.

FileStructure:
  Every .sdd file SHOULD contain:
    - Purpose
    - Owns
    - ReadOrder (if composite)
    - Modes (if applicable)
    - Rules
    - Entry
    - Navigation
    - State

ContentConventions:
  - Keep AI Core short (30-200 tokens)
  - Expand only on demand
  - Reference, don't duplicate
  - Use standard prefixes
  - Use standard states
  - Use standard relation types

Maintenance:
  - Review critical skills every 30 days
  - Review normal skills every 90 days
  - Review stable skills every 180 days
  - Trigger review on: major framework release, security advisory, breaking API, new standard, production incident

AntiPatterns:
  - Too broad skill
  - Too vague skill
  - Outdated skill
  - Contradictory skill
  - Duplicated skill
  - Unsupported skill
  - Over-engineered skill

ConventionRules:
  [CN1]  .sdd files MUST follow standard structure.
  [CN2]  Content MUST be token-efficient.
  [CN3]  Knowledge MUST be referenced, not duplicated.
  [CN4]  Anti-patterns MUST be detected and flagged.

